# Routing-and-poisoning

Telemetry-poisoning attacks on PPO-based routing agents (NSFNet-style topologies).

**Status:** TODO (fill from `docs/03_CURRENT_STATUS.md`: which stages are complete).

## Layout
- `phase1/`  original prototype, checksummed originals, original-script re-run audit
- `phase2/`  validation pipeline: `src/p2` (simulator), `src/p2x` (pipeline), `scripts/x_00..x_09`, `tests/`, `configs/`
- `phase2/results/v2/`  frozen clean-stage evidence (`freeze.json`, `SHA256SUMS.txt`, audits, final figures)
- `phase2/results/deliverables/`  poisoning/clean reports, manifests, tables
- `docs/`  protocol, threat model, methodology audit, deviations, reproduction steps
- `paper/`  manuscript sources

## Reading the results honestly
See `docs/DEVIATIONS.md` for every departure from the pre-specified protocol
(statistics revision, post-freeze code changes, pilot vs full runs).

## Reproduce
See `docs/REPRODUCING.md`. Datasets are not redistributed; see `DATA_LICENSES.md`.
